On the way home I go into a bakery.
The bread smells wonderful.
A woman stands behind the counter.
"Hello!"
"What would you like?" she asks.
"Hello."
"I would like a dark loaf of bread, please," I answer.
I like dark bread very much.
The woman takes the bread from the shelf.
Then I see the bread rolls behind the glass.
I point at a crusty bread roll.
"I would like this bread roll too, please," I say.
The bread roll is for my lunch.
The bread rolls here are not expensive.
The woman puts the food into a bag.
"That comes to four Euro and fifty cents," says the woman.
I pay and take the bag.
I go home satisfied.
